Changes made in this repository (see CHANGELOG.md, "claude-bridge" entries):

- src/agent_bridge/adapters/integration.py: added the `bridge_send` MCP tool,
  so each host can start tasks for the other host under its fixed identity;
  tool results now use the MCP CallToolResult shape, and tool errors are
  returned as readable results; every JSON-RPC notification is ignored
  without a reply; MCP stdio is forced to UTF-8 on Windows.
- src/agent_bridge/notifications.py, src/agent_bridge/permissions.py:
  helper processes (toast helper, PowerShell signing check, icacls) start
  with CREATE_NO_WINDOW on Windows, so a send no longer opens console windows.
- src/agent_bridge/setup.py: Windows toast clicks run pythonw.exe (no console
  window) when it is available.
- src/agent_bridge/paths.py: relative data roots are made absolute on
  Python 3.9 for Windows.
- pyproject.toml, tests/test_bootstrap_wheel.py: the build requires
  setuptools 77+, which the SPDX license field needs.
- .github/workflows/ci.yml, CONTRIBUTING.md: tests run with
  `discover -s tests -t .`; the Windows job installs the built wheel under
  PowerShell; shell scripts are marked executable.
- scripts/connect_claude_mcp.py (new), install.ps1, install.sh: register and
  unregister the Claude Code MCP server with `claude mcp`, which upstream
  setup did not do.
- bootstrap/: offline wheel and metadata rebuilt from the current source.
- tests/unit/test_mcp_consumer.py, tests/test_installers.py,
  tests/platform/test_windows_launcher_args.py (new): tests for the above.
- tests/support.py, tests/integration/test_cli_v2.py,
  tests/integration/test_mcp_v2.py, tests/test_mcp.py: temporary folders retry
  cleanup while the detached dispatcher still holds the database on Windows.
- scripts/build_portable_zip.py, MANIFEST.in: ship NOTICE, the Claude MCP
  helper and the instruction snippets.
- integrations/instructions/ (new): CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md instruction
  snippets for the Claude Code ⇄ Codex workflow.
- README.md, NOTICE, CHANGELOG.md, .gitattributes: documentation and line
  ending rules for this distribution.
